---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const title = 'Privacy Policy | lemonlawcalc.com';
const description = 'Privacy policy for lemonlawcalc.com — data collection, the case-review form, cookies, third-party services, and your choices.';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> July 2026</p>

  <p>Two separate things happen on this site, and this policy treats them separately: reading the calculator and guides (anonymous, nothing collected), and submitting the "Lemon Law" case-review form (collects your contact information and shares it with attorneys). Only the second one involves your personal data.</p>

  <h2>Using the calculator and guides</h2>
  <p>lemonlawcalc.com does not collect personal information from visitors who just browse the site. We do not require account registration, and all calculator inputs are processed locally in your browser — nothing you enter is transmitted to our servers.</p>
  <p>We use Google AdSense and Google Analytics. Both services may collect usage data as described in Google&rsquo;s privacy policy. Google AdSense may use cookies and device identifiers to serve interest-based advertising.</p>

  <h2>If you submit the case-review form</h2>
  <p>If you fill out and submit the "Lemon Law" case-review form on this site, we collect the information you enter &mdash; typically your name, phone number, email address, and details about your situation &mdash; along with a timestamp and record of the consent language you agreed to. <strong>This is the only way personal information leaves your browser on this site.</strong> Submitting this form is always optional; you can use the calculator and read every guide on this site without ever seeing or completing it.</p>
  <p><strong>If you submit the case-review form, your name, phone number, email address, and case details are shared with one or more attorneys or their agents licensed to practice in your jurisdiction, so they can evaluate your situation and contact you about it.</strong> The Click Lab Agency LLC, which operates lemonlawcalc.com, is not a law firm, does not provide legal advice, and does not vet, endorse, or guarantee the attorneys in this network. Submitting the form does not create an attorney-client relationship with The Click Lab Agency LLC or with any attorney until and unless that attorney separately agrees to represent you. The Click Lab Agency LLC may be compensated for these referrals. This arrangement is disclosed on the form itself at the point of submission.</p>
  <p>By submitting the form, you separately consent to be contacted by phone, text, and email &mdash; including by automated dialing technology &mdash; by The Click Lab Agency LLC and the attorneys or agents your information is shared with. That consent is not required to use any other part of this site, and you can decline it by not submitting the form.</p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>Cookies on this site are placed by Google AdSense (advertising) and Google Analytics (aggregate traffic measurement). We do not place first-party tracking cookies. Opt out of personalized Google advertising at <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Ad Settings</a>.</p>

  <h2>Third-Party Services</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Google AdSense</strong> — display advertising. Subject to <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google&rsquo;s Privacy Policy</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Google Analytics</strong> — aggregate traffic analysis. We do not use it to identify individual visitors.</li>
    <li><strong>Attorneys or their agents</strong> — receive case-review form submissions only, and only if you submit the form. See above.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your choices and opt-outs</h2>
  <p><strong>The simplest opt-out for the attorney-sharing described above is not to submit the case-review form.</strong> Nothing about your visit is shared with any attorney unless you complete and submit it yourself. If you&rsquo;ve already submitted the form and want to stop being contacted, email <a href="mailto:hey@theclicklab.agency">hey@theclicklab.agency</a> with the subject line <code>[OPT-OUT]</code>, or visit <a href="https://theclicklab.agency/optout" target="_blank" rel="noopener">theclicklab.agency/optout</a>. We will notify the attorney or agent your information was shared with and remove you from further outreach on our end.</p>
  <p>Opt out of personalized Google advertising at <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Ad Settings</a>.</p>

  <h2>California residents (CCPA/CPRA)</h2>
  <p>Sharing your case-review form information with attorneys in exchange for compensation may constitute a "sale" or "share" of personal information under the CCPA/CPRA. You have the right to opt out &mdash; the easiest way is not submitting the case-review form; to exercise this right after submission, email <a href="mailto:hey@theclicklab.agency">hey@theclicklab.agency</a> with the subject line <code>[CCPA OPT-OUT]</code>. We do not sell or share data collected only through anonymous site browsing.</p>

  <h2>EEA / UK residents (GDPR)</h2>
  <p>The legal basis for processing case-review form data is your consent, given at the point of submission, which you can withdraw at any time by emailing us. You have the right to access, correct, delete, restrict, or port your data &mdash; email <a href="mailto:hey@theclicklab.agency">hey@theclicklab.agency</a> with the subject line <code>[PRIVACY REQUEST]</code>.</p>

  <h2>Children&rsquo;s Privacy</h2>
  <p>This site is not directed to children under 13, and the case-review form is not intended for use by anyone under 18. We do not knowingly collect information from children.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>We may update this policy when our practices change &mdash; especially anything affecting the case-review form. The "Last updated" date at the top will reflect any updates.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions? Email <a href="mailto:hey@theclicklab.agency">hey@theclicklab.agency</a>.</p>
</BaseLayout>
